<section class="support-statement"><span class="statement-number">01</span><h2>Good tools should not need to squeeze students for attention.</h2><p>We want LockIn to be useful without ads, engagement tricks, or selling the context of someone’s school life. Support lets us spend more time on reliability, moderation, accessibility, and the quiet details that make a shared workspace feel good.</p></section>
<section id="ways-to-help" class="support-ways"><div class="support-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">WAYS TO HELP</p><h2>There is more than one way to show up.</h2></div><div class="support-card-grid"><article class="support-card card-coral"><span class="support-card-index">01</span><i data-lucide="log-in"></i><h3>Use it for real work</h3><p>Create your desk, bring a class or group into it, and tell us what helps. A living product is built by people actually using it.</p><a href="/">Open LockIn <i data-lucide="arrow-up-right"></i></a></article><article class="support-card card-navy"><span class="support-card-index">02</span><i data-lucide="share-2"></i><h3>Pass it along</h3><p>Share LockIn with a classmate, study group, teacher, or school network that could use a calmer coordination space.</p><a href="/about">Learn what we are building <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></a></article><article class="support-card card-gold"><span class="support-card-index">03</span><i data-lucide="message-square-heart"></i><h3>Give useful feedback</h3><p>Tell us what is confusing, missing, slow, or unexpectedly helpful. Specific feedback is one of the most valuable forms of support.</p><a href="/about">See our goals <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></a></article></div></section>
<section class="support-bottom"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT SUPPORT PROTECTS</p><h2>More care in the places you can feel.</h2></div><ul class="support-list"><li><i data-lucide="shield-check"></i><span><strong>Strict moderation</strong> so shared spaces stay respectful and usable.</span></li><li><i data-lucide="lock-keyhole"></i><span><strong>Privacy-minded infrastructure</strong> without ads or student data sales.</span></li><li><i data-lucide="accessibility"></i><span><strong>More accessible workflows</strong> for the messy, everyday work around school.</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="support-final"><p>Keep the room useful.</p><a class="button primary" href="/">Start with your desk <i data-lucide="arrow-up-right"></i></a></section>